WEBVTT

00:00:00.469 --> 00:00:05.165
Welcome to Alaventra. Rank in
search. Get recommended by AI.

00:00:06.143 --> 00:00:10.743
In tutorial 11.11, you'll give
your client their own sign-in,

00:00:10.793 --> 00:00:14.743
to follow their websites and reports
without seeing your other clients.

00:00:15.803 --> 00:00:20.310
First, open your client's workspace, go
to Company settings, and choose Team.

00:00:21.273 --> 00:00:24.873
Everyone listed here sees this
workspace as their portal.

00:00:24.923 --> 00:00:27.999
Your agency's owners and
admins reach it already.

00:00:28.938 --> 00:00:32.404
Click Invite people, and type
your client's e-mail address.

00:00:33.963 --> 00:00:37.463
Then choose a role. A Client
viewer sees the dashboards,

00:00:37.513 --> 00:00:43.100
reports and recommendations. A Client
approver also approves pages and outreach.

00:00:44.091 --> 00:00:47.441
Click Create invitation.
Then click Copy link,

00:00:47.491 --> 00:00:49.798
and send it to your client
from your own e-mail.

00:00:50.791 --> 00:00:55.683
The link is shown only once, and your client
signs in with that same e-mail address.

00:00:56.667 --> 00:01:00.467
Your client opens the link, and
clicks Create an account to join,

00:01:00.517 --> 00:01:02.327
or I already have an account.

00:01:03.321 --> 00:01:07.378
Once they've joined, they open the
company, and land in their own portal.

00:01:08.318 --> 00:01:13.513
They see their websites, from the Overview
to Rankings, AI visibility and Backlinks,

00:01:13.563 --> 00:01:17.522
plus their Reports and Approvals.
Nothing of your other clients.

00:01:18.555 --> 00:01:21.730
Now your client follows their
own results in their portal,

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:26.746
approvers can say yes to pages and pitches,
and your other clients stay private.

00:01:27.765 --> 00:01:31.980
So, open the client's Team, choose
viewer or approver, send the link,

00:01:32.030 --> 00:01:33.597
and see your client's portal.

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:39.077
You've finished the course. Next, open
your Overview, and put it all to work.
